# ============================================================================
# VELLUM CITY  (university city, 26x24 blocks, buffer 960/1300) johto_modern
# ============================================================================
# HOOK: Johto's university town. Vellum University's Great Library holds the
#   oldest records in the region (Ruins of Alph / Unown lore, legend texts),
#   the Pokemon Research Institute is where Elm and Oak once lectured, and
#   the Observatory on Campus Hill is tracking a returning comet. The city is
#   a campus first: buildings ring a formal quad, the town grew south of it
#   along Quill Lane (students' shops) and around Varsity Lake. No Gym.
#
# DISTRICTS / BUILDINGS (door steps are the exit lines below)
#   Campus Hill (NW): Observatory (2x3 tower + mast/dome, radio-tower art;
#     night-only astronomer, comet event, Moon Stone / Clefairy lore),
#     Museum of Natural History (4x3; fossil hall -- a Gen-I revive desk
#     would fit here, Unown exhibit), lawn with a headbutt grove.
#   Great Library (N centre, 5x4 window block = the landmark): quiz/puzzle
#     interior over floors (answer lore questions to reach the archive);
#     Founders' plaque (77) on the forecourt.
#   Science Row (NE): Lab A (3x2, door west end) - breeding/egg research,
#     daily egg-move or IV-judge NPC; Pokemon Research Institute (4x3) -
#     professor gives a research task (Pokedex milestones -> rewards).
#     University Avenue (cols 19-20) runs from the N exit down to College St.
#   The Quad (centre): two lawns each side of the Library axis (3-wide brick
#     walk), flower beds, street trees (2f), a headbutt grove (3f x2), the
#     fenced Reflecting Pool, a cross-walk on row 9.
#   Dorms (W): Dorm A (4x2), Dorm B (4x3); trade and rival-student NPCs.
#   East side: Student Union (3x2) - cafeteria + notice board (daily tips,
#     swap item trades); Lecture Hall (3x3) - battle-class trainers you can
#     rematch daily (stand-in for a Gym-like grind).
#   College Street (row 14): brick E-W street; W and E exits.
#   Quill Lane (SW): Scholars' Inn (3x4 tower; lobby PC + paid rest, no
#     Pokemon Center), Bookshop and Cafe (glass shopfronts 20/24), three
#     market stalls, Mart, one house.
#   Varsity Lake (SE): pond with a railed south promenade, Boathouse (rowing
#     club; Surf lore / Fishing Guru), lakeside lawn.
#
# GAMEPLAY BEATS
#   1. Arrive on College Street from W or E (or University Ave from N).
#   2. Inn + Mart on Quill Lane; Bookshop sells TMs/"textbooks" (TM shop).
#   3. Library quiz -> archive key text that points to the next story site.
#   4. Institute task + Lab A: research beats, egg / IV services.
#   5. Night: Observatory opens (see _nite render), comet sighting event.
#   6. Post-Surf: Varsity Lake fishing, hidden item on the east bank.
#
# EXITS / CONNECTIONS
#   N  University Avenue cols 19-20 (steps 38-39) -> route north
#   W/E College Street row 14 (step y 28-29)       -> routes west / east
#   S  cols 12-13 (steps 24-25)                    -> route south
# TILE GAPS / UNCERTAIN
#   - No dome/telescope block: the Observatory is the Radio Tower (mast 21
#     with its dish, 22, then 25 26 / 29 2a / 2d 2e). The dish reads as a
#     dome only loosely.
#   - No statue/bench/lamp: the Founders' plaque is a 77 brick sign.
#   - Lake bottom: the 60/61/62 railed bank has no south-east corner that
#     carries the shore strip; 61 is used to the end (strip stops at the
#     land column) instead of 62.
#   - Wide buildings (5x4 library, 4x3 museum/institute) are composed from
#     Goldenrod's dept-store pieces (18 1f 19 / 27 23 28 / 10 0f 17 11 1a);
#     render clean, but the 1f/23/0f middles are repeated beyond vanilla use.
#   - 20/24 shopfronts reuse the Pokecom-Center window wall (no 5f sign).
# ============================================================================
tileset johto_modern
ref GoldenrodCity
key T=05 .=01 :=06 ,=02 *=04 h=67 o=0a ~=35 n=43 u=61 v=2f Y=3f
key (=54 ^=76 )=55 [=58 ]=59 {=60 }=62
key <=44 >=46 r=40 f=41 t=42 l=48 e=49 j=4a s=45 S=77 w=66 x=80 z=81
key R=18 M=1f N=19 A=10 D=17 Z=11 E=1a F=0f C=1c Q=1d W=1e P=1b O=16
key H=27 I=23 J=28 K=33 1=14 2=13 3=12 G=20 X=24
key a=21 g=22 i=25 m=26 y=29 q=2a d=2d k=2e
grid:
TTTTTTTTTTTTTTTTTTT::TTTTT
T,a,,Y,,v.RMMMN.,v,::RMMNT
T,g,,,*,,.HIIIJ.RMN::HIIJT
T,im,RMMN.HIIIJ.EFZ::EFFZT
T,yq,HIIJ.AFDFZ....::....T
T.dk.ADFZ::S:::::::::v,v,T
T.....,,v,,:::,,v,,::....T
TRMMN.,*,*,:::,*,*,::RMN.T
TADFZ.,,,,,:::,,,,,::ADZ.T
T....::::::::::::::::....T
TRMMN.rfft,:::,Y,Y,::RMN.T
THIIJ.<~~>,:::,,,,,::HIJ.T
TADFZ.luuj*:::*,*,*::EFZ.T
T,.v,s,,v,,:::,,v,,::.,v,T
::::::::::::::::::::::::::
TRMN.RN.RN..::.(^^^^^^)..T
THIJ.GX.GX..::.[~~~~~~]..T
THIJ::::::::::.[~~~~~~]RNT
TADZ:h:h:h::::.[~~~~~~]OWT
T...S:::::::::.{uuuuuuu..T
TRMN.RN,*,v.::.,v,*,v,*..T
TADK.OW,,,,.::.,,,,,,,,..T
T...........::...........T
TTTTTTTTTTTT::TTTTTTTTTTTT
end
